      "params": [],
      "pos": [
        38,
        1
      ],
      "data": {
        "text": "HEMIOLA AUDIO: WHOA!  DARK AMBIENT\n\nCycle Clock runs at 40 BPM. Its SECTION trigger steps a four-note bass line in a Fundamental SEQ3 (C2, Eb2, Bb1, G2) and its SECTION gate holds each note open, so every note has time to bloom.\nWhoa! plays ratio 1.5 with slow attacks and releases. Three slow LFOs move INDEX, MOD D and the delay mix through the CV inputs. CV depth is 50 % (right-click Whoa!). Reverb pre-delay is about 250 ms.\nDelay: dotted quarter, clocked by the Cycle Clock BEAT trigger. Reverb: Vast, near-full decay. \n\nTurn REV DECAY to the top to hold the tail. Try REV TYPE on Shimmer for an octave-up wash. Not yet heard in Rack when written."
      }
    }
  ],
